        "id": "toddler-puzzles",
        "kind": "invitation",
        "title": "Take a puzzle apart, and try a piece",
        "summary": "A simple puzzle can be interesting before your child can put it back together. Offer a manageable challenge and help them repeat the part they enjoy.",
        "cue": "Notice whether they are lifting pieces out, turning them, or trying to fit one into the base.",
        "detail": [
          "Davies begins with simple knob puzzles. If your child mostly removes the pieces, you can replace them so there is another chance to take them out.",
          "When a piece becomes frustrating, offer to show a slow turn or give a small cue, then see how they continue. A harder puzzle can wait. Supervise any activity with small parts."
        ],
